1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,890
A discount can win a first order or clear a shelf, if it

2
00:00:04,890 --> 00:00:06,898
stops when you want it to.

3
00:00:06,898 --> 00:00:09,407
This video shows how coupons work:

4
00:00:09,407 --> 00:00:14,929
codes, automatic discounts, buy X get Y, limits, combining rules, links and unique

5
00:00:14,929 --> 00:00:17,250
codes, and what the buyer sees.

6
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:25,930
A discount is the oldest way to win a first order, bring back

7
00:00:25,930 --> 00:00:28,061
a customer, or clear a shelf.

8
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:32,750
Done by hand, it means editing prices and remembering to put them back.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:39,480
A code that leaks, or that nobody limited, keeps discounting until somebody notices.

10
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:45,583
Coupons give you codes buyers type, discounts that apply by themselves, and buy

11
00:00:45,583 --> 00:00:49,110
X get Y offers, each with dates, limits and rules.

12
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:55,550
You decide which discounts can be used together, and every use is counted and recorded.

13
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:04,771
A coupon takes a percentage or a fixed amount off, makes shipping free,

14
00:01:04,771 --> 00:01:06,531
or gives buy X get Y.

15
00:01:06,531 --> 00:01:11,030
It can be a code the customer enters, or an automatic discount.

16
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:17,872
Dates, a usage limit, uses per customer, minimum and maximum amounts, and products

17
00:01:17,872 --> 00:01:20,710
or categories decide when it works.

18
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:25,434
Each coupon says which other kinds of discount it combines with.

19
00:01:25,434 --> 00:01:30,600
When they cannot all be used, the buyer gets the combination that takes off the most.

20
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:36,760
You can share a code as a discount link, or generate unique single-use codes.

21
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,650
Open Commerce, Coupons.

22
00:01:42,944 --> 00:01:46,207
Open Commerce, Coupons, and click Add coupon.

23
00:01:46,207 --> 00:01:48,894
The list is empty until you add one.

24
00:01:50,747 --> 00:01:52,722
Choose how it is applied:

25
00:01:52,722 --> 00:01:54,824
the customer enters a code.

26
00:01:54,824 --> 00:02:00,302
Type the Code, such as WELCOME10, and a Description, which shows on the invoice.

27
00:02:00,302 --> 00:02:03,997
Leave the Discount type on Percentage, and enter 10.

28
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:09,913
Applies to chooses the one-time amount or the first billing cycle of a subscription.

29
00:02:09,913 --> 00:02:14,277
The Usage limit is how many purchases can use the coupon, and Uses

30
00:02:14,277 --> 00:02:17,368
per customer how many times one customer can.

31
00:02:17,818 --> 00:02:21,311
Valid until sets the date the code stops working.

32
00:02:21,311 --> 00:02:24,168
Leave Enabled ticked, and click Create.

33
00:02:24,168 --> 00:02:28,296
Give public codes an end date or a usage limit, so a leaked

34
00:02:28,296 --> 00:02:30,518
code cannot keep discounting.

35
00:02:34,721 --> 00:02:37,840
A second coupon takes a fixed amount off.

36
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:43,481
Choose Fixed amount, and enter the Amount and its Currency, such as 15 dollars.

37
00:02:48,509 --> 00:02:53,211
Minimum amount is the order total below which the coupon does nothing, and

38
00:02:53,211 --> 00:02:56,679
Maximum amount the total above which it does nothing.

39
00:02:56,679 --> 00:03:00,029
Minimum quantity is how many items the order needs.

40
00:03:00,486 --> 00:03:05,293
Combines with chooses which kinds of discount can be used on the same order:

41
00:03:05,293 --> 00:03:09,046
Product discounts, Order discounts and Shipping discounts.

42
00:03:09,046 --> 00:03:12,916
A new coupon combines with nothing until you tick something.

43
00:03:13,371 --> 00:03:18,109
Under Products and categories, a coupon can be limited to some products or

44
00:03:18,109 --> 00:03:21,366
to the categories of a taxonomy, such as a brand.

45
00:03:21,366 --> 00:03:22,491
Click Create.

46
00:03:26,683 --> 00:03:30,232
Choose Automatically, on every order that qualifies.

47
00:03:30,232 --> 00:03:34,271
It needs a Description, because that is what the buyer sees.

48
00:03:34,271 --> 00:03:35,923
Its code is optional.

49
00:03:36,378 --> 00:03:38,989
Set the Discount type to Buy X get Y.

50
00:03:38,989 --> 00:03:43,604
Customer buys is how many items count, Customer gets how many are then

51
00:03:43,604 --> 00:03:48,462
discounted, and Percentage how much comes off each, with 100 meaning free.

52
00:03:48,462 --> 00:03:51,498
Times per order limits how often it repeats.

53
00:03:51,949 --> 00:03:55,815
The cheapest items the customer gets are the ones discounted.

54
00:03:55,815 --> 00:03:59,219
Combine it with shipping discounts, and click Create.

55
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,552
Open a coupon.

56
00:04:04,552 --> 00:04:08,875
Its page shows how many times it was redeemed, and its Discount link.

57
00:04:08,875 --> 00:04:13,429
Whoever opens the link gets the code taken off at checkout without typing

58
00:04:13,429 --> 00:04:14,870
it, for seven days.

59
00:04:15,330 --> 00:04:20,652
Under Share and generate codes, enter How many, up to 5,000 at a

60
00:04:20,652 --> 00:04:26,887
time, an optional Prefix such as VIP, and Uses per code, one for single use.

61
00:04:26,887 --> 00:04:28,940
Click Generate codes.

62
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:33,688
Download them as a CSV file with each code, how often it was

63
00:04:33,688 --> 00:04:35,316
used and its limit.

64
00:04:35,316 --> 00:04:40,330
Each code shares the coupon's discount and rules, and has its own uses.

65
00:04:44,512 --> 00:04:50,276
With three notebooks in the cart, the automatic discount takes the cheapest one off by itself.

66
00:04:50,276 --> 00:04:53,272
The order summary shows it by its description.

67
00:04:53,723 --> 00:04:58,739
On the Payment step, the buyer types a code in Promotion code and clicks Apply.

68
00:04:58,739 --> 00:05:02,634
A code that cannot be combined stays in the box, with a note

69
00:05:02,634 --> 00:05:05,053
naming the discount it gave way to.

70
00:05:05,511 --> 00:05:09,077
A buyer can add up to five codes and remove each one.

71
00:05:09,077 --> 00:05:13,911
The order and its confirmation email show every discount next to its name.

72
00:05:18,085 --> 00:05:22,359
Commerce, Coupons lists your coupons, newest first.

73
00:05:22,359 --> 00:05:26,707
Search by code or description, and filter by status:

74
00:05:26,707 --> 00:05:29,705
Active, Not available or Disabled.

75
00:05:30,157 --> 00:05:34,811
Each coupon shows its discount, what it applies to, how many times it

76
00:05:34,811 --> 00:05:36,858
was used, and its end date.

77
00:05:36,858 --> 00:05:41,697
A warning appears when a code has neither a usage limit nor an end date.

78
00:05:42,154 --> 00:05:44,976
A coupon's page lists its recent uses:

79
00:05:44,976 --> 00:05:49,594
when, whether it was used, held at checkout, let go or given back,

80
00:05:49,594 --> 00:05:51,582
and how much it took off.

81
00:05:51,582 --> 00:05:54,084
To pause a coupon, clear Enabled.

82
00:05:58,284 --> 00:05:59,753
A welcome offer:

83
00:05:59,753 --> 00:06:04,764
a percentage off the first order, with a usage limit and an end date.

84
00:06:05,514 --> 00:06:07,708
A sale that runs itself:

85
00:06:07,708 --> 00:06:13,194
an automatic discount, or buy two get one free, with no code to type.

86
00:06:13,944 --> 00:06:15,681
Cards and emails:

87
00:06:15,681 --> 00:06:19,684
unique single-use codes, one for each customer.

88
00:06:20,434 --> 00:06:22,174
A free shipping weekend:

89
00:06:22,174 --> 00:06:26,004
a free shipping coupon that combines with product discounts.

90
00:06:28,004 --> 00:06:34,257
Create a code, add limits, let automatic discounts run themselves, and see every use.

91
00:06:34,257 --> 00:06:36,044
Thanks for watching.

